## 2. GGUF Split: Shard Validation Error Messages

**Component:** `include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp` — `gguf_split_paths()`.

**Responsibilities:** Resolves the shard filenames of a split GGUF model from any shard path. Throws when a shard is missing.

**Problem:** The function checks `any.size() != at + 4 + 5 + 5` which assumes the extension is exactly `.gguf` (5 chars). A file named `model-00001-of-00002.GGUF` (uppercase) or with a trailing space would silently return `{any}` (treated as single-shard), then the caller would open only one shard and miss tensors. The `std::ifstream` existence check is correct but the filename pattern is too strict.

**Proposed change:**

```diff
--- a/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
+++ b/include/strata/artifact/gguf_split.hpp
@@ -18,12 +18,16 @@ inline std::vector<std::string> gguf_split_paths(const std::string& any) {
     static const char tag[] = "-of-";
     const size_t at = any.rfind(tag);
-    // "...-NNNNN-of-MMMMM.gguf": five digits before the tag, five after it, then the extension
-    if (at == std::string::npos || at < 6 || any[at - 6] != '-' || any.size() != at + 4 + 5 + 5 ||
-        any.compare(at + 9, 5, ".gguf") != 0)
+    // "...-NNNNN-of-MMMMM.gguf" (case-insensitive extension): five digits before the tag,
+    // five after it, then ".gguf" or ".GGUF".
+    if (at == std::string::npos || at < 6 || any[at - 6] != '-')
         return {any};
+    const size_t ext_start = at + 4 + 5;
+    if (any.size() < ext_start + 5)
+        return {any};
+    const std::string ext = any.substr(ext_start, 5);
+    if (ext != ".gguf" && ext != ".GGUF" && ext != ".Gguf" && ext != ".gGuf")
+        return {any};
     int no = 0, n = 0;
     for (size_t i = 0; i < 5; ++i) {
         const char a = any[at - 5 + i], b = any[at + 4 + i];
```

**Verification cases:**
1. **Uppercase extension:** `model-00001-of-00002.GGUF` with all shards present. `gguf_split_paths` must return 2 paths, not `{any}`. Test: create a temp directory with two files named with `.GGUF`, call the function, assert `out.size() == 2`.
2. **Missing shard with correct name:** `model-00001-of-00003.gguf` exists but `model-00002-of-00003.gguf` does not. The function must throw with the message naming the missing shard. Test: `gguf_split_test` with a directory containing only shards 1 and 3 of 3.

